      Referenced so this project's own bin output contains their DLLs and ModuleAssemblies can find
      them by name. As each new module project is created (Identity.Contracts, Hr.Domain, ...), add its
      ProjectReference here too - a module assembly that isn't referenced here is invisible to every
      rule that scans by naming convention, so the rule constraining it silently stays vacuous.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\SharedKernel\SharedKernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\..\src\BuildingBlocks\BuildingBlocks.csproj" />
